[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,4.0);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.6,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.38*\x*\x});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,2.0) {Interest earned};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph shows the interest earned when money is invested at a compounding interest rate.
Which phrase correctly describes how the interest is changing?

