[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\begin{scope}[xshift=0cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,2.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(2.6,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:2.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.42*\x*\x});
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.5,1.2) {Subscribers};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (1.3,-0.5) {Time};
\node[font=\small] at (1.3,-1.1) {Service P};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[xshift=4.2cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,2.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(2.6,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:2.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-0.41*(\x-2.2)*(\x-2.2)+1.984});
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.5,1.2) {Subscribers};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (1.3,-0.5) {Time};
\node[font=\small] at (1.3,-1.1) {Service Q};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Graphs P and Q show the number of subscribers to two streaming services over the same period, both starting and ending at similar numbers.
Which service's subscriber growth is speeding up over time?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.3]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,1.2);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (4.4,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.4*\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue] (1.4,0.784) -- (2.2,0.784);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+2.2},{0.784*exp(-0.6*\x)});
\node[font=\small] at (0.7,0.3) {A};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,0.95) {B};
\node[font=\small] at (3.4,0.55) {C};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.7,0.6) {Website visitors};
\node[font=\small] at (2.2,-0.45) {Time since launch};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph shows the number of website visitors after a product launch, in three labelled stages.
During which stage is the number of visitors increasing at an increasing rate?

